                "asynchronous_ai_overview": false,
                "markdown": "Aleph (א) is the `first letter of the Hebrew alphabet` , with a numerical value (gematria) of 1.[[1]](https://www.hebrew4christians.com/Grammar/Unit_One/Aleph-Bet/Aleph/aleph.html)[[2]](https://www.chabad.org/library/article_cdo/aid/137073/jewish/Aleph.htm)\n\n### Key Facts\n\n- **Pronunciation** : It is a silent letter whose sound depends on the vowel attached to it, or it represents a glottal stop.[[1]](https://www.chabad.org/library/article_cdo/aid/137073/jewish/Aleph.htm)[[2]](https://www.timesofisrael.com/spotlight/hebrew-lesson-of-the-week-letter-aleph/)\n- **Origin** : Its ancient pictograph was an ox head, representing strength, power, and leadership.[[1]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TOW3rCmEzhU&t=13)[[2]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-G8sQU6lOCk&t=16)\n- **Structure** : In standard script, it is made of an upper *Yud* (representing God), a lower *Yud* (representing humanity), and a diagonal *Vav* (representing faith or the Torah connecting them).[[1]](https://gabrielelevy.com/pages/the-letter-aleph)[[2]](https://www.chabad.org/library/article_cdo/aid/137073/jewish/Aleph.htm)\n- **Symbolism** : It symbolizes the unity and oneness of God, and begins important words like *El* (mighty one) and *Av* (father).[[1]](https://www.levhaolam.com/blog/hebrew-language-and-literature/aleph-hebrew-letter-meaning-necklace/)[[2]](https://www.hebrew4christians.com/Grammar/Unit_One/Aleph-Bet/Aleph/aleph.html)[[3]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TOW3rCmEzhU&t=13)\n- **Tradition** : In Jewish tradition, the Torah begins with the second letter (*Bet* ), while Aleph is honored by starting the Ten Commandments with the word *Anochi*.[[1]](https://www.timesofisrael.com/spotlight/hebrew-lesson-of-the-week-letter-aleph/)[[2]](https://www.levhaolam.com/blog/hebrew-language-and-literature/aleph-hebrew-letter-meaning-necklace/)\n\nRead more about its background on [Chabad.org](https://www.chabad.org/library/article_cdo/aid/137073/jewish/Aleph.htm) or [Hebrew4Christians](https://www.hebrew4christians.com/Grammar/Unit_One/Aleph-Bet/Aleph/aleph.html).Would you like to learn about the **next letter in the alphabet (Bet)** or explore how Aleph is used in **Hebrew words and gematria**?",
